{"name":"Cypress Garden","hex":"#667c71","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cypress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen coniferous tree with flattened shoots bearing small scale-like leaves, whose dark foliage is sometimes associated with mourning, in family Cupressaceae, especially the genera Cupressus and Chamaecyparis."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Cyprus (“type of fabric”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cypress"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cypress","blocks":[{"text":"Cypress is a common name for species in several genera in the family Cupressaceae. They grow in temperate climates and subtropical regions of Asia, Europe, and North America."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypress"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Actinostrobos_are